Hello everyone. Unstable operation of the access point on the RD-5R is not related to USB interference. It is related to a power supply sag during transmission. I tried connecting an external power supply. At 9 volts, 1.5 amps and a power of 250 mW, everything has been working stably for three hours. I do not claim that I have found a solution, but for now it works. From the battery, the port fails depending on the battery charge.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8592">UR6LRD</a> — Sun May 18, 2025 10:14 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
